ce comes from the ambient DuckBrain config, not argv. Live baseline re-measured 2026-11-20T06:31Z at HEAD 7b3ae13: `python3 auger.py recall 'xml spec' --limit 3` printed the embedding-progress line and 3 semantic hits (/auger/P-CHD-SPEC-SYSTEM/D-040, /auger/AUG176-auger-docs/AD-SPEC-003-XML-SPECS-PREAMBLE-S000, /auger/P-CHD-SPEC-SYSTEM/D-030) in 4.30s wall, so the defect still reproduces (no cache, one embed round trip) but the 9.4s figure is now 4.3s - quote the CURRENT number in the closeout rather than the historical one.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:51.024669+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-20T06:22:17Z", "foreman_note": "\n\nPM REPAIR 2026-11-16 (auger-pm tick auger-pm-2026-11-16-20-51-14): acceptance rewritten so every arm names a real path, a runnable command and a recognizable outcome; current-state probes measured on main@37a9206c before the edit. Gated with acceptance_gate.py validate (PRE-ADD GATE) before writing.\n\ncos-auger-cards 2026-11-20: DISPATCHABILITY REPAIR. This row was UNDISPATCHABLE for its entire ~80h pendency (acceptance_gate.py FAIL: unexpanded placeholders for a namespace and a query), so the row gating AUG-178 AND goal card t_35d10e68's AC3 could never be picked up no matter how healthy the lane was — the barrier was the criteria, not the gateway. Repaired to the runnable single-argument form (auger recall takes ONE positional query; namespace comes from ambient DuckBrain config), pre-validated with acceptance_gate.py validate before the write, and re-measured live at HEAD 7b3ae13: 4.30s wall, 3 semantic hits, zero cache hits. Intent unchanged and no status/priority/evidence field moved; AUG-184 still owns the systemic sweep.", "capability_tags": ["perf", "recall", "ux"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
