 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-171", "title": "smoke.sh 429 teardown path has no committed regression test (verdict e273af1b residual)", "detail": {"fingerprint": "7a079da65bcced1dd312838f38cb9b0813148f46758d0daf8d04d72e7fa4b356", "evidence": [{"run_id": "2057a615", "ts": "2026-11-20T17:46:50Z"}]}, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured by verdict e273af1b tier2 while grading REVIEW-AUGER-006: tests/smoke.sh:155-158 keeps the 429 contract (drop() once, then one re-entry when the status text contains HTTP 429, and drop() rmtree's only after a 200/404 guard), but NO committed test exercises that path — tests/test_smoke_teardown.py mentions 429 only in a docstring at :187. The evaluator proved the behaviour with an ad-hoc probe running the REAL extracted heredoc against a stub answering [429, 200] and saw the namespace removed; that probe lived in /tmp, so a future edit could break the 429 retry with nothing going red. Filed rather than left as a verdict footnote.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a committed test drives the 429 teardown path in tests/smoke.sh through the real extracted helper.\nCURRENT-STATE PROBE (reproduces the gap): grep -c '429' tests/smoke.sh prints 6 (the contract sits at lines 157-158: one re-entry when the status text contains HTTP 429) while grep -c '429' tests/test_smoke_teardown.py prints 1 - that single hit is the docstring at line 187, so no test exercises the retry. Expect those exact counts before the change.\nPOST-CHANGE ARM 1: grep -c '429' tests/test_smoke_teardown.py prints 3 or more, the extra hits being test code rather than prose.\nPOST-CHANGE ARM 2: python3 -m pytest tests/test_smoke_teardown.py -q prints 0 failed and the new 429 test is collected; that test asserts exactly TWO DELETE attempts (429 then 200) with the namespace directory absent afterwards.\nPOST-CHANGE ARM 3: a persistent-429 variant expects the directory left intact and no success reported.\nFAILIF: a third DELETE attempt, the directory removed under a persistent 429, a skip, or a collection error.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-15T16:13:43.541737+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-20T17:46:55Z", "foreman_note": "\n\nPM REPAIR 2026-11-16 (auger-pm tick auger-pm-2026-11-16-20-51-14): acceptance rewritten so every arm names a real path, a runnable command and a recognizable outcome; current-state probes measured on main@37a9206c before the edit. Gated with acceptance_gate.py validate (PRE-ADD GATE) before writing.\n\nWorker report claimed grep count 8 for 429; measured count in tests/smoke.sh is 6 before and after - the file was not modified, so the discrepancy is in the worker's grep scope, not in the deliverable. Foreman re-verified the count directly.", "capability_tags": ["teardown", "smoke", "regression"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "a2cdd76", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "worker_summary": "Landed as a2cdd76 on main (worktree /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-171, branch wt/AUG-171, base 4da3a39). Two hermetic tests in tests/test_smoke_teardown.py drive the REAL helper: _heredoc_body() extracts the ns_helper python heredoc out of tests/smoke.sh and executes it, so the 429 re-entry at smoke.sh:157-158 ('if not ok and \"HTTP 429\" in why: ok, why = drop(ns)') is the code under test. Red-proved both ways: with the re-entry condition disabled both tests fail, restored they pass. 'python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_smoke_teardown.py' -> 13 passed; '-k 429' -> 2 passed; ruff check + ruff format --check clean; smoke.sh grep count for 429 unchanged at 6 (test-only change). gitreins tier-2 verdict fd... run 2057a615 = PASS.", "evidence_run_id": "2057a615"}
