 .gitreins/history/2026-11-20/f3733f6c/verdict.json` prints QA-AUGER-13. FAILIF: any cited run id resolves to a different task id, or the cited run has no verdict file.\n\nAC4 PROOF: the fix does not delete the evidence to silence the audit — either a genuine QA-AUGER-13 verdict is cited, or the row records a none_reason explaining why no QA-AUGER-13 verdict exists, and `jq -c 'select(.id==\"QA-AUGER-13\")|{status,evidence_run_id,detail}' .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl` shows the chosen shape. FAILIF: QA-AUGER-13 loses its evidence block without a recorded none_reason, or a foreign run id is swapped for another foreign run id.\n\nScope: board row QA-AUGER-13 plus, if needed, the audit fixture/rule in scripts/audit_board_evidence.py; do not weaken the foreign-citation rule to make the row pass, and do not change other rows' evidence.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-20T10:46:37Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-26T06:11:21+00:00", "foreman_note": "PM PASS7 2026-11-20T10:56:53Z (tick auger-pm-2026-11-20-09-16-17): dispatchability repair — replaced <date>/<run> with the cited run itself (2026-11-20/f3733f6c), the run whose task_id is the defect. Criteria intent unchanged; no status/priority/commit_hash/evidence field moved. Live gate after repair: acceptance_gate.py audit reports this row passing.\n\nPM PASS7 VERIFICATION 2026-11-20T10:58:27Z (tick auger-pm-2026-11-20-09-16-17): the filed premise reproduces on the live tree at HEAD aa48674. `scripts/audit_board_evidence.py` -> `complete_rows=258 bound=114 unresolvable=1 missing=0`, `LABEL QA-AUGER-13 detail.evidence[].run_id=f3733f6c resolves to task AUG-151`, `UNRESOLVABLE QA-AUGER-13 foreign-citation: cites only verdicts for other tasks: f3733f6c->AUG-151`, `RESULT: FAIL`. CORRECTION TO AC2's BASELINE: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py -q` now reports **2 failed, 15 passed**, not the filed 1 failed / 12 passed - the second failure is test_every_bound_row_resolves_to_its_own_task with `AssertionError: complete row QA-AUGER-13 carries no machine-resolvable evidence_run_id`, i.e. the same QA-AUGER-13 shape trips the per-row binding test too. AC2's '13 passed' expectation is therefore stale: the passing count after the fix must equal the rest of the file (15 today), so judge this row on 'exit 0 and zero failures in tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py', not on a hardcoded 13. Queue position: top of the dispatchable set; every worker's guard inherits this red until QA-AUGER-13's top-level evidence_run_id / foreign citation is repaired or the audit rule is extended.\n\nPM PASS8B 2026-11-20T11:27:41Z (tick auger-pm-2026-11-20-09-16-17): dispatchability repair + premise re-verified at HEAD 01e744f. AC2's expected pass count was stale (13) — the file collects 17 tests — so it now reads 17; criterion intent unchanged. Live gate this tick: `scripts/audit_board_evidence.py` -> `complete_rows=258 bound=114 unresolvable=1 missing=0` and `RESULT: FAIL`; `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py -q` -> `2 failed, 15 passed in 5.29s`. Both failures trace to the single defect this row owns: `test_the_committed_board_audits_clean` asserts rc=0 from the audit script, and `test_every_bound_row_resolves_to_its_own_task` asserts `complete row QA-AUGER-13 carries no machine-resolvable evidence_run_id` (detail.evidence[0].run_id=f3733f6c -> AUG-151). One defect, two assertions: fixing QA-AUGER-13's citation clears both, so AC1 remains the authority.\n\nNAMED BLOCKER (foreman, 2026-11-20): the row cannot close honestly this tick and is NOT a worker failure. The audit's failure is 'QA-AUGER-13 detail.evidence[].run_id=f3733f6c resolves to task AUG-151' plus 138 complete rows reported as reason=none:no-verdict-artifact-for-task-id. There is no verdict artifact bound to QA-AUGER-13 itself, so rebinding the row's evidence to a different task's verdict would manufacture provenance; the worker exercised the negative control and correctly refused. Unblock options for the next tick/owner: (a) run a real gitreins judge for QA-AUGER-13 on current main, then bind detail.evidence[].run_id to that fresh run id; (b) rule that a QA row's provenance may cite the row whose work it verified, and encode that in the audit's contract; (c) drop QA-AUGER-13's complete status if no same-task verdict exists. Until one is chosen, hosted CI stays red on the audit test (see INT-CI-001).\n\nNAMED BLOCKER, NOT CLOSED (foreman, 2026-11-20): the dispatched worker read scripts/audit_board_evidence.py and refused to fabricate a binding - no same-task verdict artifact exists for AUG-188, and the audit's real defect is upstream of any AUG-188 code change. Measured on merged main c4cf366: complete_rows=260 bound=116 unresolvable=1 missing=0, none_reason=143 (138 = no-verdict-artifact-for-task-id, 5 = cites-foreign-verdict), 19 bound rows carry a FAILED verdict, LABEL QA-AUGER-13 detail.evidence[].run_id=f3733f6c resolves to task AUG-151 -> UNRESOLVABLE foreign-citation. Same defect is the hosted-CI red, filed INT-CI-001. Blocker owner: next tick needs a decision on whether QA-AUGER-13/AUG-151 get an honest none: binding or a re-judge; the audit input cannot be fixed by editing the audit test.\n\nCOS VERIFICATION 2026-11-21T14:55Z (card manager, board restored at 9a9d987): AUG-188's fix is LANDED BUT THE ROW IS STILL PENDING — this is a reconciliation gap, not open work. The rebind landed at b3e8f17 (2026-11-20 20:50 local, \"AUG-188: rebind QA-AUGER-13 evidence to its own verdict ar...\"). Measured at HEAD 9a9d987, all four ACs:\nAC1 PASS — `.venv/bin/python scripts/audit_board_evidence.py` prints `label_defects=0` and ends `RESULT: OK` (rows=297 verdicts=182).\nAC2 PASS — `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py -q` -> 17 passed in 1.36s.\nAC3 PASS — QA-AUGER-13 cites run 3621b077 only; `.gitreins/history/2026-11-18/3621b077/verdict.json` records task_id QA-AUGER-13 (no foreign citation remains; f3733f6c is gone from the row).\nAC4 PASS WITH A CAVEAT — a genuine QA-AUGER-13 verdict is cited rather than the evidence being deleted, so the letter of AC4 holds; BUT that verdict is `passed: false`, so the row currently rests on its own FAILING verdict. The substantive re-judge is tracked by AUG-193 (its criteria now spell out the rebind + bound_failed_verdict check). Do not read AUG-188 as having produced a passing QA grade.\n\nOwner action: the auger-foreman lane can close AUG-188 verification-only with its own evidence run id (boardctl refuses a close from outside the lane, which is why this note exists instead of a status change). No re-dispatch is needed and none should be made.\n\ncommit_hash set to tip b6b3425 for task-complete re-grade (verification-only close; premise satisfied by INT-CI-003 evidence-placement fix)\n\nVerification-only close BLOCKED at the verdict leg: premise measured stale (test_the_committed_board_audits_clean passes 17/17 + audit RESULT: OK at b6b3425, measured this tick), but boardctl complete requires an evidence run id and every judge LLM seat is drained (full probe list on AUG-211). gitreins task AUG-188 created+started, awaiting a working judge seat.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "b6b3425d60320d46939c3e7fa5eb4f065d6459d6", "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-188", "branch": "wt/AUG-188", "sessions": null, "type": "bug", "worker_summary": "Re-dispatch executed and verified. Commit b3e8f17 on wt/AUG-188, ff-merged to main, pushed, remote parity 0. Bounded arm on merged main: audit RESULT: OK (unresolvable=0, label_defects=0); tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py 17 passed (was 16+1); CI run for b3e8f17 shows the evidence-audit test GREEN (only remaining failure is INT-CI-002, pre-existing since c4cf366, now filed). Judge verdict 18d2843e (commit b3e8f17): 5/6 criteria PASS, overall FAIL on the derived disposition clause - QA-AUGER-13 bound to its own failing verdict 3621b077 instead of the re-judge-to-passing-run its REQUIRED DISPOSITION demands. Row held OPEN per fleet precedent (AUG-186 pattern): landed work + named residual. Follow-up: AUG-193 (re-judge QA-AUGER-13 in a quiet window and rebind). First dispatch attempt on the configured lane openai/gpt-6.1-terra@xkiro died at gateway session.create; re-dispatched cx/gpt-6.1-terra@9router, seat verified in state.db (19 calls, 279k tokens)."}
++ {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-189", "title": "The gate's pytest arm runs under whichever python3 is first on PATH, so a clean tree grades RED for an absent dev dependency (collection errors), not for the diff", "detail": {"fingerprint": "4b98797fdeb8085358db5aa11be836586d44a479ded90225e33ba1ba14e1c018"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "COS card-manager 2026-11-20T14:55Z, filed on the promise made by the 2026-11-20T06:45Z pass (handoff open thread 1) and re-measured before filing. Measured at origin/main c7094d9 on this host: `python3` resolves differently per shell (the agent shell gets 3.14.9 via a hermes install venv, which HAS lxml+tomllib; /usr/bin/python3 is 3.14.4 and does NOT have lxml), and tests/gate.sh calls bare `python3 -m pytest` with no interpreter selection or naming. Consequence measured today at 06:23Z and reproduced now: a board-only commit attempt ran the full gate, the pytest arm died in 3.53s with 4 collection ERRORs (lxml in tests/test_xsd_conformance.py; tomllib in tests/test_packaging.py and tests/test_packaging_wheel.py; tests/test_verdict_hygiene.py also errored), and the commit was made with hooks bypassed and the bypass disclosed in the body. Proof artifacts already on disk: .gitreins/logs/guard-20261120T062345.212554Z.log and .gitreins/logs/guard-20261120T064011.062723Z.log. The repo's own .venv (3.11.15) runs the same suite green (805 passed / 2 skipped per the AUG-151 wave note), so the RED said nothing about the tree. This is the inverse of AUG-130 (which fixed PASS-on-skipped-arm): here the gate FAILS a tree it never really tested, and the asymmetry between pass and fail is not designed, it is PATH-dependent. Filing is deliberately cheap to verify: AC1's falsifier is a --collect-only probe, not the 994s suite.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1 FALSIFIER, MEASURED 2026-11-20 AT ORIGIN/MAIN c7094d9: the gate's pytest arm inherits the ambient interpreter, so an interpreter without the dev extra turns a clean tree RED. Run `/usr/bin/python3 -m pytest -q --collect-only tests/test_xsd_conformance.py` and it prints `1 error during collection` with exit code 2 (`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'lxml'`), while `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q --collect-only tests/test_xsd_conformance.py` expects exit 0 and a collected count. FAILIF: both interpreters agree, which means the gate gained an interpreter guard and this row is already satisfied.\n\nAC2 THE GATE SELECTS AND NAMES ITS INTERPRETER: `bash tests/gate.sh` run with an ambient PATH whose first python3 lacks the dev extra prints a line naming the interpreter it chose (a checkout-local interpreter is preferred when one exists), and the same invocation over a board-only or docs-only diff ends in GATE PASS or an explicitly DEGRADED pass that names its skipped required arm, never GATE FAIL for a dependency. FAILIF: the run still fails on collection errors from an interpreter the tree does not own, or no line names the chosen interpreter.\n\nAC3 NEGATIVE CONTROL, THE FAIL-CLOSED POLICY MUST NOT REGRESS: with AUGER_ALLOW_SKIPPED_ARMS unset and an interpreter that genuinely cannot import pytest, `bash tests/gate.sh` still exits nonzero and prints GATE FAIL naming the pytest arm as a required arm that did not run (the AUG-130 policy). FAILIF: GATE PASS with the suite never executed, i.e. the interpreter selection turned a true red into a silent skip.\n\nAC4 REGRESSION TEST: a committed case in the gate's own self-test asserts the selection rule (a checkout-local interpreter wins over the ambient one) so a later edit cannot re-introduce bare `python3`. Verify: `bash tests/test_gate_mode.sh` exits 0 and its output contains a case naming the interpreter selection, and `bash tests/docs_check.sh` exits 0 so documentation of the gate still matches the script. FAILIF: both scripts exit 0 but no case in the self-test names interpreter selection, i.e. the rule is unproven by test and this AC has not landed.\n\nGATE ARM: Run `bash tests/gate.sh`; expect the summary block to name the interpreter it selected.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-20T14:37:22+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-20T17:50:23+00:00", "foreman_note": "LANDED, NOT CLOSED (foreman, 2026-11-20): commit 900de88 on main (worktree /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-189, branch wt/AUG-189, base 4da3a39). Verified in-tree before merge: tests/test_gate_mode.sh 5/5 PASS including the new 'AUG-189 interpreter selection: PASS' case, tests/docs_check.sh PASS, pytest -q tests/test_xsd_conformance.py 12 passed under .venv. 'gitreins task complete AUG-189' marked the task complete but wrote NO .gitreins/history/2026-11-20/<run>/verdict.json - the only runs for today are AUG-151 x2, AUG-186, AUG-171, AUG-155. Without an artifact I cannot bind evidence_run_id, and TR-251 forbids closing on a claim, so the row stays pending. Re-run 'gitreins task complete AUG-189' on a quiet box to produce the artifact, then close with that run id.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": null}
